# API

## Questions
{: .col-2}

### Shorthands

```elixir
security: "Is this a vulnerability?"                # Noul
kind:     {"Kind?", %{bug: "Broken", other: nil}}   # Choice, 2..255
severity: {"Severity?", ["Low", "Mid", "High"]}     # Score, 2..10
```

A string or map is a yes/no question. A map of atom labels is a choice. A list of levels is a score.

### Structs

```elixir
%Jev.Noul{instructions: q, criteria: %{true: "...", false: "..."}}
%Jev.Choice{instructions: q, criteria: %{label: "..."}}
%Jev.Score{instructions: q, criteria: ["...", "..."]}
```

Instructions and every description accept text or a JSON-encodable map.

### Normalize

```elixir
Jev.questions(kind: {...}, security: "...")
#=> %{kind: %Jev.Choice{}, security: %Jev.Noul{}}
```

Raises on an empty list, a reserved name, or bad arity.

### Reserved names

`confidence`, `probabilities`, `usage`, `model`

## Reply
{: .col-2}

### Shape

```elixir
%{
  kind: :bug,          # choice → atom
  severity: 2.4,       # score  → float
  security: 0.03,      # noul   → probability
  confidence: %{kind: 0.91, severity: 0.62},
  probabilities: %{kind: %{bug: 0.93, ...},
                   severity: %{0 => 0.1, ...}},
  usage: %{input_tokens: 812, output_tokens: 0, cost: 3.4e-5},
  model: "jev-1.13.0"
}
```

### Matching

```elixir
def handle_answer(%{security: p}, tag, s) when p > 0.5
def handle_answer(%{kind: k, confidence: %{kind: c}}, tag, s) when c > 0.85
def handle_answer(%{probabilities: %{kind: ps}}, tag, s)
def handle_answer({:error, %Jev.Error{status: 429}}, tag, s)
def handle_answer({:error, reason}, tag, s)
```

### With stdlib

```elixir
with %{kind: k, confidence: %{kind: c}} when c > 0.85 <- reply, do: act(k)
Enum.max_by(reply.probabilities.kind, &elem(&1, 1))
round(reply.severity)
```

## Server
{: .col-2}

### Define

```elixir
defmodule Triage do
  use Jev.Server

  def init(arg), do: {:ok, %{}}
  def handle_call(msg, from, s), do: {:reply, {from, state, questions}, s}
  def handle_answer(reply, from, s), do: ...
end
```

### Send to Jev

```elixir
{:reply, {tag, state, questions}, s}
{:reply, {tag, state, [questions], [model: "jev-preview"]}, s}
{:reply, {tag, state, [questions], [endpoint: :laya]}, s}
```

From any callback. The answer arrives at `handle_answer(reply, tag, s)`.

### Other returns

```elixir
{:noreply, s}
{:noreply, s, timeout | :hibernate | {:continue, term}}
{:stop, reason, s}
```

### Start

```elixir
Jev.Server.start_link(Triage, arg, name: Triage)
children = [{Triage, arg}]
```

### Answer a caller

```elixir
GenServer.reply(from, result)
```

## Transport
{: .col-2}

### Call

```elixir
Jev.HTTP.post(state, questions, opts \\ [])
#=> {:ok, reply} | {:error, %Jev.Error{} | %JSONCodec.Error{} | exception}
```

### Options

`endpoint`, `model`, `api_key`, `base_url`, `max_retries`, `receive_timeout`, `tag`

### Endpoints

```elixir
Jev.HTTP.endpoint(endpoint: :laya)
#=> %{name: :laya, base_url: "...", api_key: nil, model: "jev-latest", usd_per_million_input: 0.0, ...}
```

### Error

```elixir
%Jev.Error{status: 422, body: %{...}, request_id: "req_...", endpoint: :typesafe}
```

Retries 429 and 529 with backoff before returning.

## Configuration
{: .col-2}

### Application

```elixir
config :jev,
  api_key: "...",                     # or TYPESAFE_API_KEY
  base_url: "https://api.typesafe.ai",
  model: "jev-latest",
  max_retries: 3,
  receive_timeout: 30_000,
  usd_per_million_input: 0.042,
  req_options: []
```

### Named endpoints

```elixir
config :jev,
  endpoint: :typesafe,                # the default
  endpoints: [
    laya: [base_url: "http://localhost:8000"],
    jeff: [base_url: "...", api_key: "...", model: "...", usd_per_million_input: 0.007]
  ]
```

No key sent and zero cost unless given. Transport settings inherited.

### Test

```elixir
config :jev,
  api_key: "test",
  req_options: [plug: {Req.Test, Jev.HTTP}, retry_delay: 0]
```

## Telemetry
{: .col-2}

### Events

```elixir
[:jev, :request, :start]      # system_time
[:jev, :request, :stop]       # duration, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost
[:jev, :request, :exception]  # duration
[:jev, :answer]               # confidence, probability
```

### Metadata

`endpoint`, `model`, `questions`, `state_hash`, `tag`, `status`, `request_id`, `confidence`; per answer `name`, `type`, `answer`.
